-- title:
--   Lemma 6.1 — the extended and reverse extended auctions are admissible, with admissible cost curves
-- statement:
--   Let $\varphi$ be an admissible AMM and $M\ge0$.
--
--   1. The one-sided AMM clinching auction generated by $\widetilde C_M$ (initial price $p_0$) is an admissible target-based mechanism with unattained capacity $M+x_0$, and $\widetilde C_M$ is continuous, strictly increasing and convex on $[0,M+x_0)$, starts at zero with right derivative $p_0$, and diverges at $M+x_0$.
--   2. The reverse one-sided auction generated by $\widetilde C^{\rm rev}_M$ (initial price $1/p_0$) is admissible with unattained capacity $p_0M+y_0$, and $\widetilde C^{\rm rev}_M$ has the corresponding properties on $[0,p_0M+y_0)$ with initial right derivative $1/p_0$.
--
--   Consequently the single-run structure, exact settlement, terminal certificate and same-direction Sybil-proofness of §4 apply to both auctions of the two-sided mechanism.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: environment description σ in T = (p⋆, σ, T_σ, D_σ, X_σ) → TargetMech with T : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ; σ folded into the price argument; reason: Definition 4.1 item 2: the explicit price argument selects any clock-indexed information contained in σ; same instances
--   - reading: clock map locally absolutely continuous away from its jumps (Definition 4.2(4)) → absolutely continuous on every compact price interval of the domain on which it is continuous; reason: the source does not define the phrase further; this is its direct reading
--   - encoding: cost curve properties listed in prose → IsAdmissibleCost, which also records p0 > 0 (resp. 1/p0 > 0) and a positive capacity; reason: both extra fields hold for every admissible AMM and M ≥ 0; same instances
-- source:
--   Zhang, Li, Shi, Zhang, Xia, Han, Sybil-Proofness of Generalized Adaptive Clinching and Implications for Blockchain Mechanism Design, arXiv:2610.36629 (held copy sha256 93c5d05b…), §6.1, Lemma 6.1, p.27 (PDF p.29)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SybilClinch_chordMech
import Definitions.Def_SybilClinch_TargetMech_Admissible
import Definitions.Def_SybilClinch_IsAdmissibleCost
import Definitions.Def_SybilClinch_AdmissibleAMM_Ctil
import Definitions.Def_SybilClinch_AdmissibleAMM_CtilRev

set_option autoImplicit false

open Filter Topology Set MeasureTheory

namespace SybilClinch

/-- Zhang, Li, Shi, Zhang, Xia, Han, *Sybil-Proofness of Generalized Adaptive Clinching and Implications for Blockchain Mechanism Design*, arXiv:2610.36629 (held copy sha256 93c5d05b…), §6.1, Lemma 6.1 (The extended auction inherits the one-sided results), printed p.27
(PDF p.29), first paragraph.

For every `M ≥ 0`, the one-sided AMM clinching auction generated by `C̃_M` is an admissible
target-based mechanism with unattained capacity `M + x₀`, and `C̃_M` is continuous, strictly
increasing and convex on `[0, M + x₀)`, starts at zero with right derivative `p₀`, and diverges at
`M + x₀`. The reverse auction generated by `C̃^rev_M` is likewise admissible with unattained
capacity `p₀M + y₀`, and `C̃^rev_M` has the corresponding properties on `[0, p₀M + y₀)` with initial
right derivative `1/p₀`. -/
theorem lemma_6_1 (A : AdmissibleAMM) (M : ℝ) (hM : 0 ≤ M) :
    ((chordMech (A.Ctil M) A.p0 (M + A.x0)).Admissible ∧
      (∀ s ∈ (chordMech (A.Ctil M) A.p0 (M + A.x0)).D,
        (chordMech (A.Ctil M) A.p0 (M + A.x0)).T s.1 s.2.1 s.2.2 < M + A.x0) ∧
      IsAdmissibleCost (A.Ctil M) A.p0 (M + A.x0)) ∧
    ((chordMech (A.CtilRev M) A.p0⁻¹ (A.p0 * M + A.y0)).Admissible ∧
      (∀ s ∈ (chordMech (A.CtilRev M) A.p0⁻¹ (A.p0 * M + A.y0)).D,
        (chordMech (A.CtilRev M) A.p0⁻¹ (A.p0 * M + A.y0)).T s.1 s.2.1 s.2.2 <
          A.p0 * M + A.y0) ∧
      IsAdmissibleCost (A.CtilRev M) A.p0⁻¹ (A.p0 * M + A.y0)) := by sorry

end SybilClinch
